    "narrative": "LawDog is positioned for a high-upside day, headlined by our exposure to the Fedde matchup. **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) represent our strongest plays; both benefit from a massive +19% SP skill adjustment against the favorable xERA of Fedde, combined with a significant park factor. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** (67.68) is a core start today, as his high-leverage spot at the top of the order and a +7% platoon advantage against Pfaadt make him a key accumulator for our AVG category. We are also capitalizing on stolen base opportunities against Pfaadt; **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** all receive efficiency bumps due to his slow delivery, which is vital given our strategic focus on the league\u2019s scarcest category.\n\nOur most difficult roster management decision centered on **Daulton Varsho** (47.91), who ultimately landed on the bench. While his +10% platoon edge against McLean offered intrigue, the sheer efficiency of our current outfield and utility options\u2014particularly **Tyler Freeman** (61.82) who draws a favorable park factor\u2014pushed him below the threshold. We are monitoring **Yainer Diaz** (40.38) closely, as he represents our lowest-scoring start of the day; his matchup against Ryan is suboptimal, with a -19% SP skill penalty dragging down his base projection. While we are keeping him in for now, he is the primary candidate to be pulled for a pinch-hit opportunity if we need to chase efficiency later in the evening. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remaining on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the projected performance of the lineup provides a solid floor for this slate.",
